WEBVTT

00:50.341 --> 00:52.135
My first job at this workplace

00:52.719 --> 00:54.804
was assessing prevailing visibility.

00:56.556 --> 00:59.017
I came here every morning
at the same time,

00:59.851 --> 01:02.145
observed my targets,

01:02.645 --> 01:04.731
and calculated visibility.

01:04.814 --> 01:06.274
PREVAILING VISIBILITY

01:08.610 --> 01:10.987
MOUNT INWANG
VISIBILITY: 1.6KM

01:11.071 --> 01:12.447
BAEGUNDAE PEAK

01:12.530 --> 01:14.282
MOUNT BUGAK

01:16.659 --> 01:18.745
MOUNT BUGAK
VISIBILITY: 2.9KM

01:18.828 --> 01:20.663
The thing that surprised me the most

01:20.747 --> 01:22.332
while doing this task

01:23.374 --> 01:26.252
was that the average person's sight

01:27.170 --> 01:30.256
was still good enough to be used

01:30.340 --> 01:33.176
to assess visibility.

01:34.469 --> 01:38.014
Despite the accuracy, however,
we have to rely on equipment

01:38.097 --> 01:41.851
because our vision is so easily blocked…

01:44.771 --> 01:46.022
narrowed…

01:48.316 --> 01:49.651
and distorted…

01:55.990 --> 01:57.659
by external factors.

03:39.636 --> 03:41.346
Did you get home safe?

03:41.429 --> 03:42.555
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

03:55.276 --> 04:01.783
EPISODE 4
VISIBILITY

04:05.286 --> 04:07.288
The sky is hazy this morning.

04:07.372 --> 04:11.542
The sky has become foggy
due to the drop in temperature last night.

04:11.626 --> 04:14.587
In addition, the visibility level is low

04:14.671 --> 04:16.214
due to the increase in fine dust.

04:16.297 --> 04:18.800
We advise you to drive carefully to work.

04:43.992 --> 04:45.201
Did you sleep well?

04:49.205 --> 04:50.540
If we like each other, we can go out.

04:50.623 --> 04:51.958
If not,

04:52.959 --> 04:54.335
we won't.

04:54.419 --> 04:56.087
So what are we?

04:58.172 --> 05:00.675
What are we to you?

05:07.223 --> 05:08.933
I'm a director and you're a forecaster.

05:12.937 --> 05:15.273
I'm just your senior at work.

05:15.356 --> 05:16.482
That's all.

05:16.566 --> 05:17.567
Despite our feelings?

05:17.650 --> 05:19.610
It's a fleeting emotion.

05:19.694 --> 05:20.695
Just ignore it.

05:20.778 --> 05:23.281
But what if we regret it?

05:23.364 --> 05:25.033
That's actually better.

05:25.116 --> 05:27.118
At least that leaves
something to look back on.

05:27.201 --> 05:29.245
You want me to date another colleague?

05:29.329 --> 05:30.538
No.

05:31.748 --> 05:32.957
I can't do that.

05:33.624 --> 05:34.625
I won't.

05:37.545 --> 05:40.256
But you have feelings for me.

05:50.433 --> 05:53.853
I'm sorry you had to find out.
I apologize.

06:02.403 --> 06:03.946
I don't want to apologize.

06:04.655 --> 06:06.616
I'm not sorry that you found out

06:06.699 --> 06:08.493
about my feelings for you.

06:47.740 --> 06:50.118
Due to the thick fog,
a 14-car pileup occurred

06:50.201 --> 06:54.163
on the Jungang Expressway
in Hoengseong early this morning.

06:54.789 --> 06:57.667
We made an announcement
about the fog yesterday evening.

06:57.750 --> 07:00.920
And breaking news regarding
the fog has been up since 10 p.m.

07:01.003 --> 07:05.174
The visibility during
the collision was around 100m.

07:05.925 --> 07:07.051
How about our forecast?

07:07.135 --> 07:09.095
I believe we gave enough warning.

07:09.178 --> 07:12.014
We continuously reported
that visibility could drop to 50m

07:12.098 --> 07:14.600
due to the fog that appeared
at 2 a.m. in Hoengseong,

07:14.684 --> 07:17.937
and repeatedly advised everyone
to drive safely.

07:18.521 --> 07:20.189
Okay. That's good then.

07:21.357 --> 07:23.734
What's the number
of cumulative cases in that area?

07:24.735 --> 07:27.280
In the past three years,

07:27.363 --> 07:30.783
there were 326 cases in Daegwallyeong,
115 cases in Chuncheon,

07:30.867 --> 07:32.910
and 109 cases in Cheorwon.

07:33.619 --> 07:35.830
They should have slowed down
in an area where fogs were common.

07:35.913 --> 07:37.165
Goodness.

07:38.207 --> 07:39.667
Don't you think

07:39.750 --> 07:41.836
we should come up
with more detailed measures?

07:41.919 --> 07:45.673
I'll discuss it with the other directors.

07:47.049 --> 07:49.135
Okay. Let's begin the meeting then.

07:50.136 --> 07:52.513
We'll begin the morning meeting of May 11.

07:52.597 --> 07:53.848
Satellite Center?

07:53.931 --> 07:57.101
Last night's intense radiative cooling
in the inland area

07:57.185 --> 07:59.979
- Gosh. What a competent woman she is.
- caused the thick fog

08:00.062 --> 08:01.481
- Is she still single?
- in Gangwon Province.

08:01.564 --> 08:03.774
- She almost turned out like Ms. Oh.
- But clear skies are expected

08:03.858 --> 08:05.234
- Who?
- as the sun comes out.

08:05.318 --> 08:06.903
Assistant Director Oh Myung-ju.

08:06.986 --> 08:09.030
She used to be
a promising future director.

08:09.113 --> 08:12.033
But she married a colleague
and took two maternity leaves.

08:12.116 --> 08:14.076
Now, she'll never get promoted.

08:14.160 --> 08:16.662
What does that have to do
with Director Jin?

08:16.746 --> 08:19.582
You know Deputy Director Han
at the Office of Spokesperson?

08:19.665 --> 08:21.042
- Thick eyebrows?
- Yes.

08:22.043 --> 08:24.795
They broke up
a month before their wedding.

08:25.630 --> 08:27.757
- Isn't that better for her?
- What?

08:27.840 --> 08:29.258
She could do much better.

08:29.342 --> 08:32.220
You're right. The smarter a woman is

08:32.303 --> 08:34.388
the more capable her man should be.

08:35.181 --> 08:38.059
- How much money have you saved up?
- Darn it.

08:38.893 --> 08:40.686
It's always raining on my parade.

08:49.820 --> 08:51.864
Do you guys have nothing to write about?

08:51.948 --> 08:53.157
Gather around.

08:55.701 --> 08:56.702
All right.

08:57.745 --> 08:59.413
What's your take on this?

09:00.248 --> 09:01.499
Come on.

09:01.582 --> 09:04.460
Why do you think collisions
always occur there?

09:05.670 --> 09:06.754
Look.

09:06.837 --> 09:09.590
During the collision,
the visibility was ten meters.

09:09.674 --> 09:14.595
They could barely see that far.
But what did the forecast say last night?

09:15.721 --> 09:18.516
Korea doesn't give fog advisories.

09:18.599 --> 09:19.767
- Didn't you know?
- Right.

09:19.850 --> 09:21.519
Why don't we give them?

09:22.103 --> 09:23.104
Is it the same abroad?

09:23.688 --> 09:26.399
- No. Other countries have them.
- That's exactly it.

09:26.482 --> 09:28.734
The keyword here is "why?"

09:29.235 --> 09:31.654
Why doesn't Korea have fog advisories?

09:31.737 --> 09:34.657
Perhaps, they're taking a defensive stance

09:34.740 --> 09:36.867
to avoid any criticism.

09:37.660 --> 09:39.996
Focus on that idea
and write up a special article.

09:40.079 --> 09:41.539
Include this incident

09:41.622 --> 09:44.083
and those from the past. Okay?

09:45.084 --> 09:46.627
Aren't we pushing it too much?

09:46.711 --> 09:48.713
Is it because your husband works there?

09:48.796 --> 09:50.673
No, that's not why.

09:50.756 --> 09:52.341
Then write something.

09:52.925 --> 09:55.595
A journalist doesn't drag
their private life into work.

09:56.220 --> 09:57.430
Will that be all?

09:57.513 --> 09:58.973
Now, work. This is good.

10:01.767 --> 10:04.186
- No, I'll do this.
- Okay.

10:09.191 --> 10:10.860
Are you coming from the gym?

10:11.444 --> 10:13.779
I hurried over
after hearing about the collision.

10:13.863 --> 10:15.072
I see.

10:24.707 --> 10:26.167
Did you get home safe yesterday?

10:26.250 --> 10:27.209
Yes.

10:27.918 --> 10:31.505
By the way,
who was the woman who left first?

10:31.589 --> 10:34.175
Woman? He was with a woman?

10:35.176 --> 10:37.720
I'm not sure who you're talking about.

10:37.803 --> 10:39.639
Come on. I saw everything.

10:39.722 --> 10:41.682
I saw her leaving through the back door

10:41.766 --> 10:43.684
when we arrived there.

10:43.768 --> 10:44.810
What?

10:45.436 --> 10:47.021
Do you have a girlfriend?

10:52.568 --> 10:54.111
No. Not yet.

10:54.195 --> 10:55.112
You do have one.

10:55.196 --> 10:56.739
You can't keep a poker face.

10:56.822 --> 10:59.784
I can tell that you have a woman.

11:05.706 --> 11:07.416
We're not official yet.

11:08.167 --> 11:10.503
You broke up not long ago,
and you're dating again?

11:10.586 --> 11:12.505
How did you meet her? Was it a blind date?

11:12.588 --> 11:13.714
Or at a club?

11:14.215 --> 11:17.259
No, I met her through work.

11:17.343 --> 11:19.345
Does she work here?

11:19.428 --> 11:21.222
Do we know her?

11:21.305 --> 11:22.473
Is that true?

11:22.556 --> 11:23.599
Really?

11:24.266 --> 11:25.351
Forecaster Lee!

11:29.021 --> 11:32.066
Please submit a distribution chart
of the fog in Hoengseong

11:32.149 --> 11:33.818
organized in ten-minute intervals

11:33.901 --> 11:35.778
an hour before and after the collision.

11:38.072 --> 11:39.240
Did you not get that? Do I--

11:39.323 --> 11:40.658
No, ma'am. I did.

11:40.741 --> 11:42.868
One hour before and after the collision

11:42.952 --> 11:44.161
in ten-minute intervals.

11:44.787 --> 11:46.414
Right now, please.

11:46.497 --> 11:48.457
Yes, ma'am. I'll start right away.

11:50.084 --> 11:51.502
What was that?

11:51.585 --> 11:53.170
Was she hazing him?

11:53.254 --> 11:55.714
I think so. Did he do something wrong?

11:58.092 --> 11:59.718
DREAM REALTY

12:02.054 --> 12:04.557
- Yes?
- We have a problem.

12:04.640 --> 12:06.934
I'm afraid the contracted buyer

12:07.017 --> 12:09.603
can't go through with the purchase.

12:09.687 --> 12:10.604
Why not?

12:10.688 --> 12:12.815
There were some issues with the loan.

12:13.399 --> 12:15.401
- I see.
- What do you say?

12:15.484 --> 12:18.362
If you're in a hurry,
we could lower the price.

12:20.281 --> 12:21.699
Must I do that?

12:22.324 --> 12:24.452
You'll sell the apartment
quicker that way.

12:30.332 --> 12:33.335
Let me think about it and call you back.

13:06.994 --> 13:09.413
You know Deputy Director Han
at the Office of Spokesperson?

13:09.497 --> 13:13.167
They broke up
a month before their wedding.

13:13.250 --> 13:15.211
- Isn't that better for her?
- What?

13:15.294 --> 13:16.795
She could do much better.

13:16.879 --> 13:19.089
You're right. The smarter a woman is

13:19.173 --> 13:21.008
the more capable her man should be.

13:29.099 --> 13:31.101
What's with your writing these days?

13:31.894 --> 13:33.062
What's wrong?

13:33.145 --> 13:36.774
I know it's just an in-house publication,

13:36.857 --> 13:38.359
but still, it's too sloppy.

13:38.442 --> 13:40.027
Your previous column too.

13:40.110 --> 13:42.696
Anyone could say,
"Don't catch a cold in between seasons."

13:42.780 --> 13:45.741
Even kids could say that,
so was that necessary?

13:46.408 --> 13:47.910
You didn't say much last time.

13:48.494 --> 13:50.412
I was only lenient

13:50.496 --> 13:53.582
because you were busy
preparing for your wedding.

13:55.376 --> 13:58.045
I thought you'd get back on track,
but what is this?

13:58.128 --> 14:00.923
Goodness. You can't keep this up.

14:01.006 --> 14:02.633
I won't be lenient anymore.

14:03.384 --> 14:04.593
I wasn't being sloppy…

14:07.054 --> 14:08.514
- I'm sorry, sir.
- You talk well

14:08.597 --> 14:10.266
in front of the cameras.

14:10.349 --> 14:12.893
Can't you put in some
of that effort into your writing?

14:12.977 --> 14:14.228
I'll rewrite it, sir.

14:15.145 --> 14:16.647
Stay on your toes, will you?

14:17.231 --> 14:18.232
Yes, sir.

14:18.315 --> 14:19.650
- Okay?
- Yes, sir!

14:20.484 --> 14:21.819
Rewrite it.

14:21.902 --> 14:22.945
Gosh.

14:42.214 --> 14:43.465
Were you scolded?

14:44.008 --> 14:45.676
No, I wasn't.

14:45.759 --> 14:47.428
What was it about?

14:47.511 --> 14:49.221
I said I wasn't scolded.

14:50.848 --> 14:53.100
What is it? Why are you here?

14:54.393 --> 14:57.313
The 14-car pileup
on the expressway in Hoengseong

14:57.396 --> 14:59.356
was due to the fog.

14:59.440 --> 15:01.650
What about it? We forecasted it correctly.

15:01.734 --> 15:02.902
I know.

15:02.985 --> 15:05.613
I'd like to do an interview about that.

15:05.696 --> 15:08.407
Could you find someone
from the Chief Forecasters for me?

15:10.200 --> 15:12.077
We're busy right now. Maybe later.

15:12.161 --> 15:14.496
This is pretty urgent for me.

15:14.580 --> 15:16.582
I need to submit it by the end of the day.

15:16.665 --> 15:18.834
Don't you know how busy they are?

15:18.918 --> 15:21.253
They can't be at your beck and call.

15:21.921 --> 15:23.672
You didn't have to get irritated.

15:23.756 --> 15:25.424
You're a spokesperson for them.

15:25.507 --> 15:27.968
Am I not allowed
to ask you to find someone

15:28.052 --> 15:29.428
from your own department?

15:29.511 --> 15:31.722
- I'll…
- I'm a reporter.

15:31.805 --> 15:34.558
I get it. Just give me some time, okay?

15:34.642 --> 15:36.185
I need to take care of something--

15:36.268 --> 15:38.312
Forget it. I'll do it myself.

15:44.485 --> 15:45.694
Come on.

15:46.445 --> 15:49.156
Things are tough enough for me as it is.

15:49.239 --> 15:51.700
Why did she have to make it worse?

16:19.770 --> 16:21.689
Here's the chart you wanted.

16:21.772 --> 16:24.149
I'm not sure why you need it, though.

16:24.233 --> 16:28.570
Please refrain from small talk
during working hours, Forecaster Lee.

16:33.534 --> 16:35.119
Thank you. You can go now.

16:38.372 --> 16:39.999
What? Do you have something to say?

16:40.082 --> 16:42.251
No, ma'am. I don't.

16:49.675 --> 16:52.011
She's definitely upset over something.

16:52.094 --> 16:53.262
I know.

17:06.775 --> 17:07.818
Here you go.

17:11.739 --> 17:12.573
What's going on?

17:13.824 --> 17:16.744
- What do you mean?
- Why is she upset with you?

17:17.494 --> 17:19.621
Because I made small talk at work.

17:20.539 --> 17:23.584
I know she's not the type
who gets upset over something like that.

17:24.251 --> 17:25.335
So tell me.

17:27.129 --> 17:29.673
What are we to you?

17:30.549 --> 17:31.925
I'm a director and you're a forecaster.

17:32.009 --> 17:33.510
That's all.

17:34.887 --> 17:36.722
She's putting up a wall.

17:37.347 --> 17:39.808
And why would she need to do that?

17:40.392 --> 17:42.519
"Don't think I'm easy
because I'm the youngest director."

17:42.603 --> 17:45.230
"How dare a rookie like you
get cheeky with me?"

17:46.023 --> 17:47.107
Maybe that's it.

17:47.191 --> 17:48.776
Did you get cheeky again?

17:52.696 --> 17:55.365
I told you Headquarters didn't suit you.

17:55.449 --> 17:57.826
Right? I said
it'd be very different up here.

17:57.910 --> 17:59.078
Gosh.

18:01.080 --> 18:02.998
And we're talking about Director Jin.

18:03.082 --> 18:06.001
She's a meticulous perfectionist.

18:06.627 --> 18:07.753
You're right.

18:07.836 --> 18:10.214
She's more conservative than I thought.

18:10.297 --> 18:12.174
She's not like you who's free-spirited.

18:12.257 --> 18:13.967
I'm sure you two will keep clashing.

18:14.510 --> 18:15.886
Well, it can't be helped.

18:18.138 --> 18:19.723
Did you find a place yet?

18:19.807 --> 18:20.766
Not yet.

18:21.266 --> 18:24.394
The places I like are too expensive
and the cheap ones are too shabby.

18:25.562 --> 18:27.564
Why do you ask? Will you rent me a room?

18:27.648 --> 18:29.316
No. Never.

18:29.399 --> 18:30.901
Try harder.

18:30.984 --> 18:34.071
Also, stop being cheeky with Director Jin.

18:34.154 --> 18:36.949
And you don't have time
to date right now. Take it slow.

18:47.334 --> 18:49.920
The surface temperature
will drop again tomorrow morning

18:50.003 --> 18:52.297
due to radiative cooling, right?

18:52.381 --> 18:56.051
Yes. The temperature difference
is quite big there.

18:56.760 --> 19:00.848
We can give the same details
on the fog as we did yesterday.

19:00.931 --> 19:03.100
What if we extended the range?

19:03.183 --> 19:04.935
- Where?
- Wouldn't that be too wide?

19:05.769 --> 19:07.396
How about we break down the areas?

19:07.479 --> 19:09.189
I think we should emphasize

19:09.273 --> 19:12.568
the valleys, streams, and tunnels.

19:15.279 --> 19:18.866
Fog is the thickest
between 3 a.m. and 7 a.m.

19:18.949 --> 19:22.619
And during that time frame,
the expressway is the most populated.

19:25.581 --> 19:26.999
Back off, will you?

19:27.082 --> 19:30.460
Still, it wouldn't be effective
to encompass the entire region.

19:30.544 --> 19:33.046
Plus, route three gets a lot of sunshine.

19:33.130 --> 19:35.799
So the fog will clear up
immediately after sunrise.

19:37.092 --> 19:38.969
Why? Are you uncomfortable?

19:42.055 --> 19:45.142
According to the observational data
from yesterday,

19:45.225 --> 19:47.394
that area had high relative humidity.

19:47.978 --> 19:49.938
I know that region very well.

19:50.022 --> 19:53.275
The fog is pretty intense
at this time of year.

19:54.443 --> 19:56.486
You sure know a lot of things.

19:57.070 --> 19:59.990
You knew a lot about the West Sea
since you'd been on a weather ship.

20:00.073 --> 20:03.493
And now, you know about
the fog situation in Gangwon Province?

20:03.577 --> 20:05.954
The former is true,
and I served in Gangwon Province.

20:06.038 --> 20:09.416
I know the terrains
like the back of my hand.

20:09.499 --> 20:11.376
As for changes in climate,

20:11.460 --> 20:14.213
I've experienced them firsthand
numerous times

20:14.296 --> 20:16.506
unlike you who only looked at monitors.

20:17.257 --> 20:18.675
What are you doing right now?

20:18.759 --> 20:21.595
As a severe weather forecaster,
I'm appealing to the director.

20:27.893 --> 20:28.936
Forget it.

20:29.645 --> 20:31.730
- Let's give a comprehensive warning.
- Okay.

20:31.813 --> 20:34.608
No, we must break down the areas
and give separate warnings.

20:34.691 --> 20:36.401
Especially near the tunnels and bridges.

20:36.485 --> 20:39.029
- Forecaster Lee.
- During the hail

20:39.112 --> 20:40.364
and the rain,

20:41.281 --> 20:42.407
I was right.

20:47.621 --> 20:51.333
Judging by how most accidents
on the Hoengseong expressway

20:51.416 --> 20:53.377
occur mainly in May and June,

20:53.460 --> 20:55.128
I agree with her.

20:55.212 --> 20:56.213
Did you hear that?

20:56.296 --> 20:59.633
But if we take
the terrains into consideration,

20:59.716 --> 21:01.051
I agree with him too.

21:01.134 --> 21:03.512
- Did you hear that?
- In any case,

21:03.595 --> 21:08.308
it's a fact that Gangwon Province
will be foggy tomorrow morning.

21:08.392 --> 21:12.521
First, let's report the parts
that you've already agreed on.

21:12.604 --> 21:13.897
- What about the rest?
- And the details?

21:13.981 --> 21:15.107
You…

21:15.691 --> 21:18.068
We'll have to continue our discussion.

21:18.735 --> 21:19.945
If there's no agreement,

21:20.028 --> 21:21.822
we'll hand it over to the night team.

21:22.322 --> 21:24.032
Time's up already.

21:26.118 --> 21:26.952
Okay?

21:29.997 --> 21:30.956
Okay?

21:31.623 --> 21:32.666
This is Headquarters.

21:32.749 --> 21:34.793
We just sent you information on the fog.

21:34.876 --> 21:36.086
Did you check?

21:36.670 --> 21:37.879
I see.

21:37.963 --> 21:41.216
First, please inform that region
of the fog tomorrow morning.

21:41.883 --> 21:43.302
As for the details…

21:48.598 --> 21:51.476
I'll hand them over myself
as soon as they're ready.

21:51.560 --> 21:52.602
Goodbye.

22:04.239 --> 22:07.034
CUSTOMER SURPRISE SERVICE INDEX
CATEGORY: MATCHMAKING SERVICE

22:07.117 --> 22:09.953
SEOUL AWARD CERTIFICATE
NUBO, MATCHMAKING SERVICE

22:11.455 --> 22:14.416
Your daughter is
a Grade Five civil servant.

22:14.499 --> 22:15.584
That's correct.

22:16.293 --> 22:19.004
And that's not all.

22:19.087 --> 22:21.006
Among all the competent test-takers,

22:21.089 --> 22:23.342
she was the second one to get accepted.

22:23.425 --> 22:24.509
I see.

22:24.593 --> 22:27.596
Mom, it's not too late. Let's go home.

22:27.679 --> 22:28.764
Be quiet.

22:28.847 --> 22:30.766
Ha-kyung will be furious if she finds out.

22:30.849 --> 22:32.768
Go first if you're scared.

22:32.851 --> 22:33.935
I'm all done.

22:34.019 --> 22:35.437
How's the result?

22:35.520 --> 22:38.315
One minute. Your daughter's grade is…

22:38.398 --> 22:41.276
I'm sure she's in the top rank.

22:41.777 --> 22:43.487
Like prime beef.

22:43.570 --> 22:46.865
How could you compare her to beef?

22:46.948 --> 22:48.492
She's not some meat.

22:49.076 --> 22:50.327
Shut it!

22:53.205 --> 22:54.998
- She's Grade Eight.
- What?

22:55.749 --> 22:57.000
Grade Eight?

22:57.584 --> 23:00.504
That's actually not bad.

23:04.257 --> 23:05.342
Hold on.

23:05.425 --> 23:07.928
How could she be Grade Eight?

23:08.011 --> 23:11.181
She was always at the top of her class.

23:11.765 --> 23:14.351
As I said before,
marriage is about two families

23:14.434 --> 23:16.228
joining together.

23:16.311 --> 23:19.231
There are many factors
to take into account other than her job.

23:19.314 --> 23:21.483
One's personal information is important.

23:21.566 --> 23:24.444
But one's parents and siblings

23:24.528 --> 23:27.614
play a big role in determining the grade.

23:27.697 --> 23:28.907
Are you

23:29.699 --> 23:32.452
looking down on her
for having a single parent?

23:32.536 --> 23:35.080
No, that's not why.

23:35.580 --> 23:38.583
I'm afraid you don't have enough wealth.

23:38.667 --> 23:41.920
It's not easy for a mother
to raise two kids to begin with,

23:42.003 --> 23:44.214
so how could you expect me to be wealthy?

23:44.798 --> 23:46.049
Unbelievable.

23:46.133 --> 23:48.176
See? We should have just left.

23:48.969 --> 23:50.137
Only those whose parents

23:50.220 --> 23:52.848
have at least 20 billion won
are in Grade One.

23:55.058 --> 23:56.852
Many doctors and lawyers

23:56.935 --> 23:58.812
are in Grade Seven.

23:58.895 --> 24:03.358
Even doctors and lawyers
are in Grade Seven?

24:03.441 --> 24:05.610
Let me say this again.

24:05.694 --> 24:06.903
Grade Eight consists

24:06.987 --> 24:09.823
of employees from large companies
and civil servants.

24:09.906 --> 24:11.741
It's not that bad, ma'am.

24:11.825 --> 24:13.743
I can guarantee that we can find someone

24:13.827 --> 24:16.413
who has a similar background
to your daughter's.

24:16.496 --> 24:17.581
Let's go.

24:24.671 --> 24:25.714
All right.

24:31.261 --> 24:34.055
Now, should we come up
with a detailed plan

24:34.139 --> 24:35.849
for your daughter's marriage?

24:40.103 --> 24:42.772
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

24:44.566 --> 24:46.318
You seem to be busy all day.

24:46.401 --> 24:48.695
Yes, I'm preparing to do an interview

24:48.778 --> 24:49.988
for a special article.

24:53.366 --> 24:55.535
Why do you ask?
Do you have something to say?

24:55.619 --> 24:58.246
That forecaster from before
was Lee Si-woo, right?

25:00.457 --> 25:02.000
How did you know his name?

25:02.083 --> 25:04.169
I heard he broke up not too long ago.

25:06.254 --> 25:07.339
So?

25:08.381 --> 25:09.424
Hook me up.

25:12.219 --> 25:14.387
There's plenty of fish in the sea.

25:14.471 --> 25:17.390
Why would you want to date a colleague?

25:17.474 --> 25:18.767
People will talk.

25:18.850 --> 25:20.518
It's only dating.

25:21.186 --> 25:24.773
And I'm sick of coming here
only to write articles.

25:25.315 --> 25:27.317
I want to date someone too. Please?

25:27.984 --> 25:28.902
I'm not sure.

25:28.985 --> 25:32.280
I'm not close enough
to hook someone up with him.

25:34.783 --> 25:36.451
Reporter Chae. Hey.

25:36.534 --> 25:38.787
Wait for me.

25:52.384 --> 25:55.345
Forecaster Lee is quite popular, right?

25:56.179 --> 25:57.180
I'm not sure.

25:57.264 --> 26:00.392
I wonder. Whom could he be dating?

26:01.059 --> 26:03.228
Why are you curious about that?

26:06.064 --> 26:08.358
I think she works here.

26:09.192 --> 26:10.235
How come?

26:10.318 --> 26:12.237
He said they met through work.

26:12.320 --> 26:16.032
But that doesn't have to mean
that she works here.

26:16.116 --> 26:17.909
I saw her at the pub last night.

26:17.993 --> 26:21.162
As soon as we arrived,
she fled through the back door.

26:21.246 --> 26:23.331
It's obvious he's dating a colleague.

26:24.249 --> 26:25.333
He said they aren't official.

26:25.417 --> 26:27.627
Well, I think that's what he said.

26:28.336 --> 26:30.297
So you were listening.

26:30.380 --> 26:33.967
It wasn't intentional. I just overheard.

26:34.551 --> 26:36.803
Don't hate him too much.

26:36.886 --> 26:38.555
He's still a newbie.

26:39.180 --> 26:40.557
I never hated him.

26:42.559 --> 26:45.395
Anyway, I'll let you know
if I hear anything else.

26:46.563 --> 26:48.315
I'm dying to find out who she is.

26:56.364 --> 26:58.575
Office romance will be the death of me.

26:59.701 --> 27:00.952
THE ATMOSPHERE

27:04.664 --> 27:06.249
- See you tomorrow.
- Goodbye.

27:06.333 --> 27:07.584
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

27:09.627 --> 27:10.670
Goodness.

27:11.171 --> 27:13.965
The night team is already here.

27:14.049 --> 27:17.677
Why would you go out of your way
and write up the fog details?

27:17.761 --> 27:20.889
I told the Gangwon Office
that I'd send it to them by midnight.

27:20.972 --> 27:23.683
I said not to get cheeky,
not go out of your way to help her.

27:23.767 --> 27:26.269
I'm hoping this will
help me win her favor.

27:26.353 --> 27:27.437
Goodness.

27:27.520 --> 27:29.522
- Don't go home too late, okay?
- Okay.

27:29.606 --> 27:30.857
- See you.
- Good luck.

27:43.828 --> 27:45.205
Do you need any help?

27:46.206 --> 27:47.665
No, thank you.

27:48.583 --> 27:50.168
Really? Goodbye, then.

27:50.251 --> 27:51.252
Goodbye.

27:53.463 --> 27:54.881
Turn around.

27:55.465 --> 27:57.008
Turn around.

27:57.801 --> 27:59.010
Turn around.

28:00.845 --> 28:02.180
She didn't turn around.

28:04.265 --> 28:05.767
Darn it.

28:49.811 --> 28:50.979
Excuse me.

28:52.814 --> 28:54.357
Can you spare me some time?

28:55.442 --> 28:56.651
For what?

28:58.278 --> 28:59.904
It's for an article I'm writing.

28:59.988 --> 29:01.865
I need a director's opinion.

29:02.532 --> 29:04.784
If you're uncomfortable,
I can ask someone else.

29:14.753 --> 29:18.673
THEMED STORY FOR JUNE

29:20.300 --> 29:21.885
Are you stuck?

29:24.012 --> 29:25.096
Yes.

29:29.559 --> 29:31.311
What's this about? "May"?

29:31.394 --> 29:33.062
- That's your theme?
- Yes.

29:35.231 --> 29:36.357
Let's see.

29:36.858 --> 29:38.151
May…

29:39.360 --> 29:42.822
In May, the weather is nice
and people like to go outside.

29:42.906 --> 29:43.782
Right.

29:44.866 --> 29:48.286
How about you share tips
on how to utilize the weather forecast?

29:48.369 --> 29:49.704
- Should I?
- Yes.

29:50.622 --> 29:52.499
Then for the title…

29:52.582 --> 29:54.209
How about this?

29:55.043 --> 29:57.545
"This Coming Spring!
The Weather White Paper."

29:57.629 --> 29:58.922
- Not bad.
- Is it too cheesy?

29:59.005 --> 29:59.964
- I like it.
- Really?

30:00.048 --> 30:00.965
- Yes.
- Let's see.

30:01.049 --> 30:03.134
- "This Coming Spring!"
- "Coming Spring!"

30:03.218 --> 30:06.054
- "The Weather White Paper."
- "The Weather White Paper."

30:06.137 --> 30:08.598
Share your personal tips on how to utilize

30:08.681 --> 30:10.475
the weather forecast.

30:18.525 --> 30:20.485
THEMED STORY FOR JUNE

30:35.875 --> 30:38.336
There have been
many fog-related accidents lately.

30:39.003 --> 30:41.047
It's not limited to only recent events.

30:41.130 --> 30:42.924
The temperature range is wide
in late February,

30:43.007 --> 30:45.426
early April, mid-May,
late August, and early October,

30:45.510 --> 30:47.345
so fogs appear often in those months.

30:47.428 --> 30:49.514
And that is why accidents

30:49.597 --> 30:51.558
occur more often.

30:52.475 --> 30:54.227
But it's true that there were

30:54.310 --> 30:56.604
many fog-related accidents
in that region lately.

30:57.647 --> 31:00.483
The Seohae Bridge probably has
a similar number of accidents.

31:02.318 --> 31:03.486
By the way,

31:03.570 --> 31:06.322
why doesn't our country
give fog advisories?

31:09.033 --> 31:12.036
They're not that effective
because the fogs are very localized.

31:12.120 --> 31:14.873
To give severe fog warnings,
we need to set up equipment

31:14.956 --> 31:20.003
that can monitor
moisture particles every two kilometers.

31:20.086 --> 31:23.631
But we can't afford to do that
with the budget that we have.

31:23.715 --> 31:26.759
So you're saying it's due
to a lack of money and equipment?

31:26.843 --> 31:28.261
You're not just choosing not to?

31:31.639 --> 31:33.766
What is it that you want to hear?

31:34.392 --> 31:36.144
I'm just looking for the facts.

31:38.605 --> 31:41.858
The recent collision
in Hoengseong happened

31:41.941 --> 31:45.570
because the drivers' visibility
dropped due to the fog.

31:46.362 --> 31:49.490
It's not that our forecast
of the fog was incorrect.

31:50.074 --> 31:51.117
Those are the facts.

31:51.200 --> 31:54.037
That's up to the public to judge.

32:04.339 --> 32:05.882
How are you at home?

32:05.965 --> 32:07.425
Well…

32:08.468 --> 32:10.637
- I'm okay.
- Really?

32:10.720 --> 32:11.721
Yes.

32:12.347 --> 32:15.016
I see. Still, it's going
to be awkward for some time.

32:15.975 --> 32:17.185
Hold on.

32:17.268 --> 32:18.853
Were you like this too?

32:20.813 --> 32:22.398
You know me.

32:22.482 --> 32:25.360
I hated being away from my family,

32:25.443 --> 32:28.404
so I always brought them with me
wherever I was dispatched.

32:28.488 --> 32:31.074
- Right.
- I think it was in my second year.

32:31.157 --> 32:34.410
I had to go somewhere alone
because my kid was preparing for college.

32:34.494 --> 32:35.745
I see.

32:35.828 --> 32:37.956
And after I went back home,

32:38.665 --> 32:41.376
it took a while to fully settle in.

32:41.459 --> 32:43.878
Right? This is normal, right?

32:44.462 --> 32:46.714
That's not what I'm getting at.

32:46.798 --> 32:49.842
I'm telling you to take more initiative.

32:49.926 --> 32:53.680
Okay? If you keep distancing yourself
because you feel awkward,

32:53.763 --> 32:56.265
then you're bound to become an outsider.

32:56.349 --> 32:57.350
Understand?

32:58.935 --> 33:00.937
I didn't mean I was one.

33:01.020 --> 33:03.982
- Anyway, keep that in mind.
- All right.

33:05.942 --> 33:09.362
How long will it take for me

33:09.445 --> 33:11.364
to finally settle in?

33:11.447 --> 33:13.199
One to two months? Half a year?

33:13.282 --> 33:14.784
That depends on you.

33:16.369 --> 33:17.537
Right.

33:36.222 --> 33:37.473
What are you doing?

33:45.023 --> 33:46.274
It must be something funny.

33:49.569 --> 33:50.987
What is it?

33:52.071 --> 33:54.407
Why are you looking at my phone?

33:55.324 --> 33:56.743
I didn't see anything.

33:59.746 --> 34:01.956
And so what if I do? We're family.

34:12.508 --> 34:14.093
Gosh.

34:26.522 --> 34:29.192
Do you need help with anything?

34:29.275 --> 34:30.359
I'm fine.

34:31.069 --> 34:32.987
This one? Let me help.

34:36.824 --> 34:39.869
- Goodness.
- You're unbelievable!

34:40.703 --> 34:42.955
You should have just stayed put.

34:43.039 --> 34:45.583
Why would you try to help me
and cause a ruckus?

34:45.666 --> 34:48.086
I was only trying to help.

34:48.169 --> 34:50.671
You can only help if you know how to.

34:50.755 --> 34:52.632
You don't know how to manage a house.

34:55.134 --> 34:58.679
Don't you think you guys
are being too harsh on me?

34:59.847 --> 35:02.850
Fine. I'm sorry that we had
to live apart for 14 years.

35:03.851 --> 35:05.561
But we had no choice.

35:06.687 --> 35:09.607
Did I want to move out? Did I?

35:09.690 --> 35:13.486
We just couldn't afford to move around.

35:14.237 --> 35:16.697
It wasn't like
I was seeing other women either.

35:17.323 --> 35:19.283
I always provided for you two.

35:19.367 --> 35:21.536
Then don't you think you could have said,

35:22.120 --> 35:23.913
"Thank you. Welcome home."

35:23.996 --> 35:26.457
You could have
at least said something nice.

35:27.041 --> 35:29.335
If I were a dog,
you'd be happy to see me again.

35:29.418 --> 35:31.838
Must I walk on eggshells around you guys?

35:35.341 --> 35:37.093
- Are you done?
- Yes.

35:38.094 --> 35:40.096
Do you think earning money for us

35:40.179 --> 35:43.516
and not cheating on your wife
makes you a good husband?

35:44.100 --> 35:47.061
Then what else? What more do I need to do?

35:48.020 --> 35:50.356
Where were you when Bo-mi was born?

35:52.400 --> 35:53.693
When she was born…

35:53.776 --> 35:55.153
I was--

35:55.236 --> 35:57.488
You were aboard
a weather ship in the South Sea.

35:58.072 --> 36:01.450
You finally got to see her
when she was well over 100 days old.

36:01.534 --> 36:04.287
Right. But there was nothing I could do.

36:04.370 --> 36:06.706
What about during
her elementary entrance ceremony?

36:07.874 --> 36:09.750
I was…

36:09.834 --> 36:13.254
You sent a single text
from Baengnyeong Island.

36:14.005 --> 36:16.591
I know. I had explained it to you.

36:16.674 --> 36:18.593
The situation back then

36:18.676 --> 36:20.887
didn't allow me to come here.

36:20.970 --> 36:22.847
Again, you had no choice.

36:24.932 --> 36:26.017
Did you know?

36:27.310 --> 36:31.606
There was a time when our neighbors
thought I was a single mother.

36:31.689 --> 36:32.815
What?

36:33.566 --> 36:35.234
Who thought that?

36:35.318 --> 36:36.402
Everyone did.

36:37.236 --> 36:38.905
Everyone in this neighborhood.

36:40.114 --> 36:41.616
When Bo-mi was sick,

36:41.699 --> 36:44.994
I carried her on my back
and rushed her to the hospital.

36:45.828 --> 36:48.372
When I took her to the supermarket,

36:48.456 --> 36:50.750
they'd give me
free products because they thought

36:50.833 --> 36:52.376
I was raising her by myself.

36:54.337 --> 36:56.505
I didn't know what to say.

36:57.632 --> 36:59.258
You were crazy about the weather

36:59.342 --> 37:02.470
that you were always
at sea or in the mountains.

37:02.553 --> 37:04.347
You were so busy

37:04.430 --> 37:06.432
that you'd only come home
every now and then.

37:06.515 --> 37:08.601
And the next morning, you'd be off again.

37:08.684 --> 37:10.394
Were you ever there for Bo-mi?

37:10.478 --> 37:11.729
Were you?

37:15.149 --> 37:17.026
That was how Bo-mi and I lived

37:17.985 --> 37:19.820
for the past 14 years.

37:21.697 --> 37:23.532
Do you get that, Dong-han?

38:15.918 --> 38:19.130
THEMED STORY FOR JUNE

38:41.694 --> 38:44.280
MESSAGE FROM SPACE
AN INTRODUCTION TO DYNAMIC METEOROLOGY

38:44.363 --> 38:47.158
THE ENCYCLOPEDIA
OF WEATHER AND CLIMATE CHANGE

38:58.669 --> 39:00.129
THOSE WHO FIGHT AGAINST WEATHER

39:00.212 --> 39:03.341
"Those Who Fight Against Weather."
"By Chae Yu-jin."

39:10.181 --> 39:11.766
How adorable.

39:25.112 --> 39:26.947
What's wrong?

39:27.656 --> 39:30.368
Isn't he that psycho from our wedding?

39:30.451 --> 39:33.579
No. I think you're mistaken.

39:34.580 --> 39:35.706
Are you sure?

39:36.374 --> 39:38.042
It was definitely not him.

39:57.686 --> 40:00.147
WHY DOESN'T KOREA…

40:17.957 --> 40:19.875
Goodness, you startled me!

40:23.212 --> 40:25.881
- She'll probably get mad, right?
- Yes.

40:28.384 --> 40:30.678
Maybe I should have asked
before signing her up.

40:30.761 --> 40:32.138
Seriously?

40:33.097 --> 40:35.683
That was what I kept telling you

40:35.766 --> 40:37.768
while following you around all day.

40:37.852 --> 40:39.478
That we should ask her first.

40:40.438 --> 40:41.897
I did it for her.

40:41.981 --> 40:43.566
No, you did it for yourself.

40:43.649 --> 40:45.693
You're embarrassed
to tell others about her,

40:45.776 --> 40:48.612
so you're desperately trying
to marry her off to a decent man.

40:48.696 --> 40:50.698
You little brat.

41:05.045 --> 41:06.380
Did you get home safe?

41:10.259 --> 41:11.927
Yes. Where are…

41:13.888 --> 41:15.014
No.

41:15.097 --> 41:17.308
I have to speak formally.

41:19.059 --> 41:20.644
Forecaster Lee.

41:21.395 --> 41:23.522
Thank you for your hard work today.

41:24.023 --> 41:25.399
Are you still at…

41:27.860 --> 41:29.111
Never mind.

41:30.362 --> 41:31.947
Never mind.

41:39.705 --> 41:40.581
LEE SI-WOO

42:07.316 --> 42:09.193
He's crazy about the sky.

42:18.285 --> 42:20.120
- How do I turn this off?
- Director Jin?

42:20.829 --> 42:23.040
Hello, Forecaster Lee. How's work?

42:23.123 --> 42:25.584
It's going well. I'm almost done.

42:25.668 --> 42:27.378
Why did you call?

42:27.461 --> 42:30.839
Well, I just wanted to know
how the work was going.

42:30.923 --> 42:33.717
Come on. Did you think
I'd bail and not do the work?

42:34.343 --> 42:35.970
No, I wasn't doubting you.

42:36.595 --> 42:39.056
If that's not it, did you miss me?

42:40.474 --> 42:41.559
Don't get cheeky.

42:41.642 --> 42:44.061
Then why did you call this late at night?

42:44.144 --> 42:47.064
Well, I want you to find cases
from countries around the world

42:47.147 --> 42:50.901
that frequently have fogs like we do
and put them on my desk.

42:51.569 --> 42:53.153
- What?
- And find out

42:53.237 --> 42:55.406
which countries have fog advisories,

42:55.489 --> 42:59.285
what equipment they use,
and their budgets.

43:00.286 --> 43:01.704
Are you serious?

43:02.871 --> 43:04.123
Do I look like I'm joking?

43:05.249 --> 43:07.001
No, ma'am.

43:07.793 --> 43:10.713
Okay. I better see them
when I get to work tomorrow.

43:10.796 --> 43:12.798
- Goodbye.
- Yes, ma'am.

43:16.802 --> 43:18.762
Okay. That was smooth.

43:20.222 --> 43:21.473
What was that?

43:22.391 --> 43:24.184
Why is she putting up such a high wall?

43:30.649 --> 43:33.819
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

43:34.445 --> 43:35.571
Goodness.

43:38.532 --> 43:40.492
- Hey.
- Hello.

43:41.994 --> 43:43.245
What's all this?

43:43.329 --> 43:47.041
Director Jin told me to look up countries
that frequently had fogs as well

43:47.124 --> 43:50.336
and those that gave fog advisories.

43:51.337 --> 43:53.422
So you pulled an all-nighter?

43:53.505 --> 43:55.591
It doesn't really matter
whether I sleep here

43:55.674 --> 43:57.009
or at the training center.

43:57.635 --> 44:01.180
Hey, don't smile like that.
You're breaking my heart.

44:01.263 --> 44:04.141
You have terrible dark circles right now.

44:04.224 --> 44:06.810
It's okay.
She said she needed these reports.

44:07.686 --> 44:09.146
Do you really think so?

44:10.064 --> 44:11.649
These useless theses?

44:11.732 --> 44:12.691
What?

44:14.026 --> 44:16.612
- Are you thinking what I'm thinking?
- Yes.

44:17.696 --> 44:19.948
- What is it?
- There's this thing

44:20.032 --> 44:23.994
a senior does to teach
their cheeky subordinate a lesson.

44:24.953 --> 44:27.081
In other words, she's wasting your time.

44:28.248 --> 44:29.083
No way.

44:29.750 --> 44:32.086
That can't be. Come on.

44:35.172 --> 44:37.132
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

44:43.389 --> 44:44.723
Is something wrong?

44:44.807 --> 44:47.351
No, ma'am. Nothing's wrong.

44:51.438 --> 44:52.481
What's all this?

44:52.564 --> 44:54.817
These are the reports
you asked for last night.

44:56.902 --> 44:59.780
By the way, you really needed them, right?

45:00.531 --> 45:01.615
Did I waste my time?

45:02.616 --> 45:04.785
Of course not. Let me see.

45:04.868 --> 45:07.663
Director Jin, you need to see this.

45:07.746 --> 45:08.914
What is it?

45:23.637 --> 45:24.930
Hey, Mr. Han.

45:25.722 --> 45:27.182
Are you serious?

45:29.268 --> 45:30.602
WHY DOESN'T KOREA HAVE FOG ADVISORIES?

45:30.686 --> 45:33.147
INCOMPETENT KMA BLAMES IT ON TIGHT BUDGET!

45:35.441 --> 45:36.775
REPORTER CHAE YU-JIN

45:38.861 --> 45:40.612
Did you really not know?

45:48.162 --> 45:50.456
I'm sorry, sir. I wasn't aware.

45:50.539 --> 45:53.917
How could you not know
what your wife was writing?

46:27.910 --> 46:30.037
- What is this?
- It's an article.

46:31.288 --> 46:33.916
This wasn't what I said yesterday.

46:34.541 --> 46:37.211
A reporter shouldn't distort the facts.

46:37.794 --> 46:39.505
Exactly which part was distorted?

46:39.588 --> 46:40.464
I told you

46:40.547 --> 46:43.133
that we aren't simply choosing
not to give fog advisories.

46:43.217 --> 46:44.718
And that's what I wrote.

46:44.801 --> 46:46.136
What's the problem?

46:47.971 --> 46:50.140
I don't think you understand.

46:50.224 --> 46:53.227
Taebaek and Hamgyong Mountains
lean toward the east,

46:53.310 --> 46:57.105
and it's a tilted block where the east
has a steep slope, while the west is flat.

46:57.189 --> 47:00.108
The straight line
from Seoul to Wonsan is long and narrow.

47:00.192 --> 47:02.653
It's the same shape
as the Chugaryeong Tectonic Valley.

47:02.736 --> 47:03.862
So?

47:03.946 --> 47:04.821
So what?

47:06.907 --> 47:08.742
Do you still not get it?

47:08.825 --> 47:10.452
Meteorologists from around the world

47:10.536 --> 47:13.038
say that the country with
the most difficult conditions

47:13.121 --> 47:15.666
when it comes to observing
the weather is right here,

47:15.749 --> 47:17.125
the Republic of Korea.

47:17.209 --> 47:19.378
It's a peninsula
where 70 percent is mountainous.

47:19.461 --> 47:22.005
We have 11 major rivers and 1,206 dams.

47:22.089 --> 47:24.841
Plus, fogs are very localized.

47:24.925 --> 47:27.928
So I said we didn't give advisories
because they weren't effective.

47:28.011 --> 47:31.515
So how could you denounce us
by saying that we're incompetent?

47:33.141 --> 47:34.351
Oh, please.

47:34.851 --> 47:37.396
I thought you lacked the equipment for it?

47:37.479 --> 47:39.606
Lack of money and equipment
due to a tight budget.

47:39.690 --> 47:43.735
That's an excuse
every government department often gives.

47:45.320 --> 47:47.739
- Excuse?
- It's true.

47:47.823 --> 47:50.158
Your yearly budget
is over 400 billion won.

47:50.242 --> 47:52.494
Do you think our citizens will understand

47:52.578 --> 47:54.621
if you blame it on a lack of equipment?

47:54.705 --> 47:56.164
Wouldn't it be a lame excuse?

47:57.082 --> 47:59.251
Other countries all have fog advisories.

47:59.334 --> 48:00.377
Give me an example.

48:00.460 --> 48:01.878
The UK, the US,

48:01.962 --> 48:03.380
- Australia, and Japan.
- The UK?

48:04.756 --> 48:06.925
Do you know what their yearly budget is?

48:07.009 --> 48:08.969
It's 1.6 trillion won.

48:09.052 --> 48:10.679
That's four times more than us.

48:10.762 --> 48:12.180
The US? Japan?

48:12.264 --> 48:13.515
- Australia?
- Whatever.

48:13.599 --> 48:15.475
You should have at least read

48:15.976 --> 48:17.644
some theses beforehand.

48:17.728 --> 48:18.937
If not…

48:21.023 --> 48:23.567
you should have cross-checked
with someone you knew.

48:29.656 --> 48:32.409
Did you know about this
and turn a blind eye?

48:33.243 --> 48:36.496
Did you want me to suffer
due to your personal feelings?

48:48.634 --> 48:49.551
It's my fault.

48:50.844 --> 48:52.679
I'll take care of it.

48:52.763 --> 48:54.264
You can go back to work, Director Jin.

48:58.894 --> 49:00.103
You better do a proper job

49:01.813 --> 49:03.357
of dealing with the press.

49:11.281 --> 49:12.491
You'll take care of it?

49:12.574 --> 49:14.743
Let's go somewhere quiet.
We can talk there.

49:16.370 --> 49:17.621
Take care of what?

49:18.246 --> 49:19.748
The mess you've created!

49:19.831 --> 49:21.875
I should take care of it
since I'm in charge!

49:26.088 --> 49:28.048
You should've done your research
before going up against her.

49:28.131 --> 49:32.135
Ha-kyung beat all the competition
and became the youngest director.

49:32.219 --> 49:33.512
So what?

49:34.096 --> 49:37.724
You confused probability of detection
with accuracy when you first came.

49:37.808 --> 49:39.267
Yet you picked a fight with--

49:39.351 --> 49:40.811
Why are you bringing that up?

49:40.894 --> 49:43.772
You should have at least
discussed it with me beforehand.

49:43.855 --> 49:46.441
So I asked you
to find someone to interview yesterday.

49:46.525 --> 49:50.070
And I told you to wait! I could have
proofread it if you were unsure!

49:50.654 --> 49:51.488
Why?

49:52.072 --> 49:54.408
Reporters don't ask
their subjects to proofread.

49:54.491 --> 49:56.201
I'm a journalist.

49:56.284 --> 49:59.204
It's my job to keep an eye on you
and hold you in check.

50:01.873 --> 50:03.083
Don't be ridiculous.

50:03.166 --> 50:04.960
You're neither logical nor factual.

50:05.043 --> 50:06.753
All you do is ridicule your subjects.

50:06.837 --> 50:09.673
- Ki-jun.
- Why did you lie if you're so great?

50:09.756 --> 50:10.966
Lie?

50:11.049 --> 50:12.467
I never lied.

50:12.551 --> 50:13.552
Lee Si-woo.

50:15.679 --> 50:17.013
You said you didn't know him.

50:26.398 --> 50:27.774
Are you sure about that?

50:48.420 --> 50:50.464
I think she's getting an earful.

50:51.131 --> 50:53.759
I know.
Why did she have to do the interview?

50:54.634 --> 50:57.637
How could she have declined?

50:57.721 --> 51:01.057
Then people would think
she was still bitter about the breakup.

51:02.684 --> 51:06.438
This is why breaking up
with a colleague is painful.

51:06.938 --> 51:09.483
But then again, marrying a colleague

51:09.566 --> 51:11.735
isn't something to brag about either.

51:22.996 --> 51:24.039
I'm sorry.

51:24.623 --> 51:26.458
She needed help with her article.

51:26.541 --> 51:29.294
I should have been
more careful with my words.

51:29.377 --> 51:30.587
I don't want to hear it.

51:32.881 --> 51:35.509
So? Did you give her an earful?

51:37.093 --> 51:38.929
Yes. I was enraged.

51:40.055 --> 51:40.972
Well done.

51:43.058 --> 51:46.394
The reporters bash us
all the time without good reasons.

51:46.478 --> 51:47.938
We should speak our minds.

51:48.688 --> 51:51.733
Think about it.
Even though we're known for being patient,

51:52.317 --> 51:55.487
we should correct them
if they get their facts wrong.

51:56.363 --> 51:57.614
Good job.

51:58.240 --> 52:00.283
Right. Speaking of which,

52:01.034 --> 52:02.828
I want you to write up a report.

52:04.371 --> 52:07.916
Provide reasons why our country

52:07.999 --> 52:10.168
doesn't give fog advisories.

52:10.752 --> 52:12.587
We can't openly refute the article,

52:12.671 --> 52:15.048
so let's write a feature story.

52:15.632 --> 52:17.843
- Okay?
- Yes, sir.

52:37.404 --> 52:38.822
Why are you here?

52:43.660 --> 52:47.080
Our director just told me
that you're writing

52:47.831 --> 52:49.165
a refuting feature article.

52:50.375 --> 52:51.585
So?

52:52.168 --> 52:54.254
How long will it take?

52:54.963 --> 52:57.507
I'm not sure.
There's a massive amount of data.

52:58.091 --> 53:01.428
I'd appreciate it
if you could give me your rough draft.

53:02.220 --> 53:03.346
I need it

53:04.556 --> 53:06.391
to write up the rebuttal.

53:10.145 --> 53:11.688
Did you really not know about it?

53:19.821 --> 53:22.407
No, I didn't.

53:25.619 --> 53:27.037
I thought marriage meant

53:27.120 --> 53:30.206
communicating and sharing
more with each other.

53:31.207 --> 53:32.834
I guess I was wrong.

53:35.462 --> 53:37.547
I'll give you the draft
by tomorrow morning.

53:37.631 --> 53:38.548
Goodbye.

53:57.817 --> 53:59.402
What? She did what?

54:00.570 --> 54:04.199
She signed you up
for a matchmaking service.

54:06.242 --> 54:07.953
I did it for you.

54:08.036 --> 54:10.497
You were acting like a complete fool.

54:11.373 --> 54:13.375
I couldn't tolerate it any longer,

54:13.458 --> 54:17.712
so I'm going to find a man
who's suitable with you--

54:19.047 --> 54:20.632
See? I told you.

54:22.467 --> 54:24.844
This is all for your sake.

54:24.928 --> 54:27.138
Imagine if you got married

54:27.222 --> 54:28.974
to a successful man.

54:29.057 --> 54:31.434
Your stature at work would grow.

54:31.518 --> 54:33.979
Is that bastard, Ki-jun,
getting in the way?

54:34.062 --> 54:35.647
I'm right, aren't I?

54:36.231 --> 54:37.899
I don't think you are.

54:38.525 --> 54:40.568
Know when to go along with me, you brat.

54:52.122 --> 54:54.499
- Ha-kyung, what's all that?
- What?

54:54.582 --> 54:57.210
- I think she's leaving.
- What?

54:57.293 --> 54:58.628
Are you serious?

54:59.671 --> 55:02.716
Delete all my data
from the matchmaking service

55:02.799 --> 55:04.300
and unsubscribe.

55:04.384 --> 55:05.885
I'll come back then.

55:06.594 --> 55:08.888
Hey, I spent a lot of money on that.

55:11.057 --> 55:12.267
- Ha-kyung.
- Hey!

55:12.350 --> 55:14.102
- Ha-kyung! Gosh.
- What did I tell you?

55:14.185 --> 55:15.186
That little…

56:53.993 --> 56:57.163
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

56:57.247 --> 56:59.415
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

57:03.586 --> 57:06.005
Hello, Director Jin. What's the matter?

57:06.089 --> 57:08.466
- Were you sleeping?
- No, not yet.

57:08.550 --> 57:09.968
Thank goodness.

57:10.051 --> 57:12.470
I'm looking at
the English case you analyzed.

57:12.971 --> 57:15.974
I think the translations are a bit off.
Can you help me?

57:26.192 --> 57:27.235
Which part?

57:27.318 --> 57:29.070
Page 12.

57:29.154 --> 57:31.156
The second chapter.

57:31.239 --> 57:32.866
Okay. One minute.

57:34.075 --> 57:35.201
I see.

57:45.837 --> 57:47.338
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

57:49.841 --> 57:50.758
Hello?

57:51.426 --> 57:53.720
Page 27, Table 3-1.

57:53.803 --> 57:55.555
Do you have a graph for that?

58:08.902 --> 58:10.153
Yes?

58:10.236 --> 58:12.614
Do you think we can use the Sydney case?

58:13.198 --> 58:14.616
It has too many singularities.

58:18.703 --> 58:20.121
Are you listening?

58:20.747 --> 58:23.416
Yes, I am. One minute.

59:04.165 --> 59:05.208
Why are you here?

59:05.291 --> 59:07.669
Because you keep calling
every five minutes.

59:07.752 --> 59:09.504
We last spoke 30 minutes ago.

59:09.587 --> 59:11.798
Staying up this late made me hungry,

59:11.881 --> 59:13.508
so I came out to eat.

59:13.591 --> 59:15.218
And I thought you'd be hungry too.

59:19.847 --> 59:21.140
Come in.

59:24.644 --> 59:25.728
Here.

59:29.607 --> 59:31.568
Oh, there are two different toppings.

59:32.485 --> 59:33.403
What's wrong?

59:33.987 --> 59:36.155
I don't like having
two different toppings.

59:37.991 --> 59:39.993
In that case, here.

59:40.994 --> 59:42.704
We can

59:43.955 --> 59:45.665
put two slices together.

59:49.669 --> 59:50.670
Is it good?

59:52.547 --> 59:53.548
Try some.

59:55.008 --> 59:56.384
- Like this?
- Yes.

59:56.467 --> 59:59.304
- Put them together?
- Yes, together.

01:00:00.013 --> 01:00:01.306
Then eat it.

01:00:01.389 --> 01:00:02.557
- Like this?
- Yes.

01:00:04.434 --> 01:00:05.518
Isn't it good?

01:00:06.394 --> 01:00:07.770
Eat up.

01:00:22.994 --> 01:00:25.455
This is from
the Meteorological Office in the UK.

01:00:25.538 --> 01:00:28.333
There should be
the original copy of the article in there.

01:00:28.416 --> 01:00:29.834
- Can you find it?
- Sure.

01:00:31.961 --> 01:00:34.881
I've highlighted
the important parts in blue.

01:00:37.300 --> 01:00:39.344
I think we should break it down.

01:00:39.427 --> 01:00:42.180
- Like that?
- Yes. It's a bit difficult to explain.

01:00:42.263 --> 01:00:43.806
So let's add that.

01:00:47.101 --> 01:00:48.811
I think it's pretty much done.

01:00:49.395 --> 01:00:50.521
What do you think?

01:01:09.457 --> 01:01:11.834
But you have feelings for me.

01:01:14.045 --> 01:01:15.588
I'm sorry you had to find out.

01:01:16.339 --> 01:01:17.548
I apologize.

01:01:22.095 --> 01:01:23.429
I don't want to apologize.

01:01:25.223 --> 01:01:26.724
I'm not sorry that you found out

01:01:27.225 --> 01:01:28.851
about my feelings for you.

01:01:32.480 --> 01:01:33.898
Because they're genuine.

01:03:00.109 --> 01:03:02.069
What? I thought you left already.

01:03:02.153 --> 01:03:04.489
No, I had some work to do.

01:03:05.072 --> 01:03:07.992
I heard Lee Si-woo is already
in a new relationship.

01:03:10.536 --> 01:03:11.704
What do you mean?

01:03:12.872 --> 01:03:15.041
Everyone knows about it already.

01:03:15.625 --> 01:03:17.960
He's dating a colleague.

01:03:30.264 --> 01:03:31.933
Isn't it so pretty?

01:03:33.434 --> 01:03:34.685
It is.

01:03:35.686 --> 01:03:37.772
This is my favorite time of the day.

01:03:38.397 --> 01:03:40.316
So you're a morning person.

01:03:42.777 --> 01:03:43.986
What else?

01:03:50.284 --> 01:03:53.412
I'm not going to put this place
on the market just yet.

01:03:56.874 --> 01:03:58.376
I'll be reminded of my past,

01:03:58.960 --> 01:04:01.629
but I'm hoping to make new memories here.

01:04:05.800 --> 01:04:07.051
What else?

01:04:08.135 --> 01:04:10.054
What? What more do you want to know?

01:04:10.680 --> 01:04:11.848
Everything.

01:04:12.598 --> 01:04:16.561
I want to know
every single thing about you.

01:04:17.228 --> 01:04:18.479
Everything.

01:04:21.941 --> 01:04:23.359
I told you to be discreet.

01:04:24.110 --> 01:04:25.945
We're not at work.

01:04:28.114 --> 01:04:29.949
You know that it's over for us

01:04:30.032 --> 01:04:32.285
if our colleagues find out, right?

01:04:33.995 --> 01:04:35.121
I do.

01:04:36.581 --> 01:04:40.543
And I'll have to keep putting up walls
between us in front of them.

01:04:42.086 --> 01:04:43.254
I'm also

01:04:44.171 --> 01:04:45.464
aware of that.

01:04:48.718 --> 01:04:52.889
Visibility is the maximum distance
that can be seen with the naked eye.

01:04:52.972 --> 01:04:54.265
Do you have a girlfriend?

01:05:02.565 --> 01:05:04.275
No. Not yet.

01:05:05.026 --> 01:05:07.570
- Right now, please.
- Yes, ma'am. I'll start right away.

01:05:07.653 --> 01:05:09.989
What was that? Was she hazing him?

01:05:10.072 --> 01:05:12.491
I think so. Did he do something wrong?

01:05:22.543 --> 01:05:26.380
But depending on the environment,

01:05:27.423 --> 01:05:29.300
this distance can easily
be blocked from view.

01:05:29.383 --> 01:05:33.763
Please refrain from small talk
during working hours, Forecaster Lee.

01:05:34.430 --> 01:05:36.015
Thank you. You can go now.

01:05:36.933 --> 01:05:37.975
It can be narrowed.

01:05:39.685 --> 01:05:41.646
What? Do you have something to say?

01:05:41.729 --> 01:05:43.481
No, ma'am. I don't.

01:05:47.401 --> 01:05:48.819
And it can be distorted.

01:05:50.363 --> 01:05:53.157
I'm never going to date
a colleague ever again.

01:05:53.240 --> 01:05:54.492
I know.

01:05:55.493 --> 01:05:57.620
I think we should emphasize

01:05:57.703 --> 01:06:00.915
the valleys, streams, and tunnels.

01:06:11.217 --> 01:06:13.094
As for now,

01:06:13.177 --> 01:06:16.639
this is the visibility that only we have.

01:06:18.307 --> 01:06:21.519
What if others find out about us?

01:06:22.561 --> 01:06:25.147
Then we'll have to break up.

01:06:26.148 --> 01:06:27.525
Oh.

01:06:28.192 --> 01:06:29.318
How thrilling.

01:06:30.611 --> 01:06:33.489
I don't want to go through
another breakup like that.

01:06:34.115 --> 01:06:35.324
Okay?

01:07:04.061 --> 01:07:07.273
At times, we may encounter bad weather

01:07:07.356 --> 01:07:11.235
such as thick fog,
yellow dust, rain, or snow.

01:07:46.645 --> 01:07:48.022
But through those moments,

01:07:49.148 --> 01:07:50.649
we'll learn something.

01:07:54.904 --> 01:07:58.491
That the best way to narrow our visibility

01:07:59.116 --> 01:08:03.954
is by mustering the courage
to take a step closer to each other.

01:08:25.559 --> 01:08:26.477
I'm late.

01:08:46.413 --> 01:08:47.540
Wait for me.

01:08:48.124 --> 01:08:50.209
- No, you leave later.
- But aren't we late?

01:08:50.292 --> 01:08:51.168
No, you are.

01:08:59.218 --> 01:09:00.427
THE EFFECTIVENESS OF FOG ADVISORIES
AND CASES FROM ABROAD

01:09:23.826 --> 01:09:24.994
Hello?

01:09:53.355 --> 01:09:55.983
How did you cross paths
with Director Jin this morning?

01:09:56.066 --> 01:09:57.484
- We met on our way here.
- Pardon?

01:09:57.568 --> 01:09:58.402
It was a coincidence.

01:09:58.485 --> 01:10:01.363
Who said you could
keep crossing lines like that?

01:10:01.447 --> 01:10:03.866
Did you want to see
how I would react if I saw him?

01:10:03.949 --> 01:10:06.035
Call me outside like this
one more time and I'll…

01:10:06.118 --> 01:10:06.952
Forecaster Lee, you--

01:10:07.036 --> 01:10:09.163
Do you know of a heart
that asks for permission to beat?

01:10:10.080 --> 01:10:11.957
Get it together, Forecaster Lee!

01:10:12.541 --> 01:10:13.709
It's the Metropolitan Office.

01:10:13.792 --> 01:10:15.920
They're saying the rain echo
over Seoul looks abnormal.

01:10:16.003 --> 01:10:17.296
Could you take a look?

01:10:22.343 --> 01:10:26.889
Subtitle translation by: Soo-ji Kim
